4. Layers of spring boot
Controller: how the application respond to a api. It gets http requests and return responses
Service: defines the business logics
Entity: map to specific database
Repository: defines how to interact with database
DTO: transfer data between layers

5. Describe the flow in all of the layers if an api is called
The client side send a http request, the controller gets the request, for example if I want to get an user
by id. The request first arrive at the controller, then controller pass it to the service layer, then the
service layer interact with repository to find the user. After finding it, database send the response to
service and then to controller and finally back to the client.

6. application.properties, application.yml
It is the configuration file for a spring boot app. I can define properties like server settings, database
connections, logging, security. application.yaml provides more readable structure than application.properties

7. Naming differences between GraphQL and rest API? why is the difference?
Graphql has a single endpoint while rest has multiple endpoints. Graphql uses query types for methods, query,
mutation, subscription. Rest uses http methods, get, post, delete. Graphql is more flexible than rest, it can
fetch related data in a single query. They are for different purpose, rest is to get predefined structure of
data and graphql is for more flexible requests.

8. How graphql solve N+1 problems in rest.
If we want to fetch a list of items from api, we need to send multiple requests. But we can do it in a single
query with graphql. For example, we can get all posts and also authors id. We can get all users and their followers id.








